00:15.490 --> 00:18.240
<b></b>Message

00:15.490 --> 00:18.240
<b></b>Now

00:15.490 --> 00:18.240
<b></b>First stop, Cambodia

01:58.510 --> 02:01.260
I'll do that. And I'll
save up money.

01:58.510 --> 02:01.260
It'll be my immediate goal.

01:58.510 --> 02:01.260
First stop, Cambodia

01:58.510 --> 02:01.260
Safe travels.

02:01.670 --> 02:05.090
<i>I wonder if Itsuomi-san's reached Cambodia yet.</i>

02:06.020 --> 02:09.400
Do you have a passport?

02:06.020 --> 02:09.400
I don't. I do want to try
going overseas, though.

02:06.020 --> 02:09.400
Get one, and I'll
take you.

02:09.480 --> 02:12.020
I'll do that. And I'll
save up money.

02:09.480 --> 02:12.020
It'll be my immediate goal.

02:09.480 --> 02:12.020
First stop, Cambodia

02:09.480 --> 02:12.020
Safe travels.

02:13.370 --> 02:16.020
<i>I want to be able to travel with him...</i>

02:16.600 --> 02:19.310
<i>so I gotta hurry up and find a job!</i>

02:22.670 --> 02:26.340
<i>I... I can't read her lips.</i>

02:23.490 --> 02:26.370
<b>Interview in Progress</b>

02:23.490 --> 02:26.370
<b>Please maintain silence.</b>

02:27.750 --> 02:30.250
<b>Chuo-dori</b>

02:30.650 --> 02:33.380
<i>They're probably not going to call me.</i>

02:33.900 --> 02:36.760
<i>I wonder how people normally 
find part-time work.</i>

02:40.630 --> 02:45.010
<i>I'm pretty sure this was the place 
Madoka-chan mentioned in high school...</i>

02:46.070 --> 02:49.520
I'm gonna work here for sure!

02:51.270 --> 02:53.020
<b>Use this space to list why you want to work here, your hobbies, your skills, etc.</b>

02:53.550 --> 02:54.530
Boom!

02:55.020 --> 02:56.910
<i>She did get accepted here.</i>

02:57.650 --> 02:58.900
Yoohoo!

02:57.650 --> 02:58.900
Madoka-chan, would you mind
giving me advice on something?

02:57.650 --> 02:58.900
I've been thinking of
starting a part-time job
during spring break...

02:58.820 --> 03:02.410
Madoka-chan, would you mind
giving me advice on something?

02:58.820 --> 03:02.410
I've been thinking of
starting a part-time job
during spring break...

02:58.820 --> 03:02.410
Could you give me some pointers
on the process?

03:04.930 --> 03:07.160
<i>Wow, she responded already?</i>

03:07.160 --> 03:10.160
Thanks for letting me
stay the night, Rin-chan.

03:07.160 --> 03:10.160
No problem. See you
at college!

03:07.160 --> 03:10.160
Today

03:07.160 --> 03:10.160
Yuki <3 Are you free
to meet right now?

03:07.610 --> 03:09.570
<i>Hmm? Rin-chan?</i>

03:10.160 --> 03:13.540
Man, work's killing me!

03:13.920 --> 03:21.300
You started working too?

03:15.420 --> 03:17.650
Yeah, at a realtor's office.

03:17.650 --> 03:21.300
It's been busy, probably 
because it's spring break.

03:22.120 --> 03:24.260
Fujishiro-san! Run a listing check!

03:24.260 --> 03:25.480
Listing check?!

03:25.480 --> 03:27.560
That's the meter box, not storage!

03:27.560 --> 03:28.750
I'm sorry!

03:28.750 --> 03:30.110
Answer the phone!

03:30.110 --> 03:31.310
On it!

03:33.000 --> 03:33.810
Hey there.

03:34.530 --> 03:36.970
No need to panic and rush things, 
okay, Rin-chan?

03:36.970 --> 03:39.900
Thank you, Tsujimura-san!

03:39.900 --> 03:42.260
If there's anything you don't understand, 
feel free to ask.

03:42.770 --> 03:45.900
Thank you so much...

03:47.350 --> 03:49.080
How about you?

03:49.390 --> 03:51.790
Found a job yet?

03:54.080 --> 04:05.340
Not yet. It's been hard.

03:55.750 --> 03:57.160
Oh...

03:57.160 --> 03:59.300
When does Itsuomi-san get back, again?

04:00.590 --> 04:05.340
End of spring break, apparently.
He's visiting a bunch of countries.

04:02.680 --> 04:05.340
Haha, that's so him.

04:05.860 --> 04:09.770
Must be nice to have a boyfriend 
who's used to going overseas, though.

04:10.330 --> 04:11.350
<i>Boyfriend...</i>

04:11.600 --> 04:15.100
So, I can call him
my boyfriend?

04:13.490 --> 04:15.100
What else would he be?

04:15.450 --> 04:20.500
He might not be around at the moment, 
but you two have started dating.

04:21.480 --> 04:24.360
You can develop your love once he gets back.

04:25.080 --> 04:26.110
<i>Love...</i>

04:27.100 --> 04:28.440
<i>Love, huh?</i>

04:34.540 --> 04:36.130
Isn't it great?

04:36.580 --> 04:39.130
<i>Okay, I'm going to keep at it!</i>

04:39.130 --> 04:41.630
<b>Job Details</b>

04:39.130 --> 04:41.630
<b>No Phone Calls!</b>

04:39.130 --> 04:41.630
<b>Daily Pay OK</b>

04:39.130 --> 04:41.630
<b>Short-Term College Students Welcome!</b>

04:39.130 --> 04:41.630
<b>Simple Data Entry Staff</b>

04:39.130 --> 04:41.630
<b>[1,700 yen/hr] F&B Reservation Entry
Thrice a Week OK!</b>

04:44.130 --> 04:46.970
Could you give me some
pointers on the process?

04:44.130 --> 04:46.970
Some places may not
be disability-friendly

04:46.800 --> 04:50.390
Try to overcome that with your cover letters.
And then just apply to a bunch
of different places.

04:50.850 --> 04:53.640
The worst they can say is no!

04:50.850 --> 04:53.640
-by Madoka

04:58.650 --> 05:01.150
<b>Thank you for applying to us...






...decided that you would not be a good fit...





...ask for your understanding...</b>

05:01.150 --> 05:03.650
<b>Thank you for
taking the time.</b>

05:03.650 --> 05:06.160
<b>After much careful consideration...
...unfortunately have to pass...
It's truly unfortunate...
...please understand.</b>

05:08.660 --> 05:10.410
<b>The result was, unfortunate...
...decided to go with a different candi...
We apologize...</b>

05:10.410 --> 05:12.160
<b>...decided to go with a diff...
It pains us to inform...
...hope to hear from...</b>

05:12.160 --> 05:13.910
<b>unfortunately</b>

05:16.750 --> 05:20.950
<i>I can't get a job at all. 
Is it really this hard?</i>

05:26.430 --> 05:29.050
Oushi

05:26.430 --> 05:29.050
I added you. Yay.

05:26.430 --> 05:29.050
Today

05:26.430 --> 05:29.050
What's up?
You at home?

05:27.060 --> 05:29.170
<i>Hmm? Oushi-kun?</i>

05:28.970 --> 05:31.930
What's up?
You at home?

05:28.970 --> 05:31.930
My sister's back home for a bit.

05:32.530 --> 05:35.230
<i>His sister? Mio-san?</i>

05:36.680 --> 05:38.060
Yuki-chan!

05:40.560 --> 05:42.190
<b></b>It's been ages

05:40.560 --> 05:42.190
<b></b>It's been ages

05:43.150 --> 05:49.220
<i>Mio-san studied sign, and we 
used to play together as kids.</i>

05:51.090 --> 05:55.650
You've grown up so pretty! 
I love your hair color.

05:55.650 --> 05:57.570
Use sign, Mio.

05:57.570 --> 05:58.210
Oh.

06:00.190 --> 06:03.910
Right... Sorry, I've forgotten most of it.

06:05.180 --> 06:07.100
Interpret for me, Oushi.

06:07.100 --> 06:08.040
Wha?

06:09.670 --> 06:13.480
I'm working at a nursing home.

06:13.480 --> 06:19.000
We had a deaf person move in recently, 
which made me think of you.

06:29.950 --> 06:32.520
We talked a bunch! That was fun.

06:32.520 --> 06:34.160
Thanks, Oushi.

06:34.160 --> 06:34.910
Sure.

06:34.910 --> 06:37.080
Teach me stuff again.

06:37.080 --> 06:40.070
Oh, can we exchange contact details?

06:41.940 --> 06:44.620
Thanks. I'll read the QR code.

06:46.260 --> 06:49.170
Let's video call and stuff sometime.

06:53.000 --> 06:55.860
But, really, you're amazing, Oushi.

06:56.730 --> 06:59.080
You've been consistent in your 
sign language studies.

07:00.750 --> 07:02.440
Not translating that?

07:02.770 --> 07:03.420
Huh?

07:03.850 --> 07:05.710
You wouldn't, would you?

07:10.700 --> 07:12.110
happy to be friends

07:10.700 --> 07:12.200
<b>Good to know you.</b>

07:12.110 --> 07:13.700
Yuki-chan, you're
in love, aren't you?

07:18.080 --> 07:22.620
How did you know?

07:19.830 --> 07:22.710
It's obvious! You look so
much prettier now, too.

07:22.580 --> 07:25.210
I can lend you an ear
anytime if you wanna
talk about it  <3

07:28.410 --> 07:32.740
You go to the same college, right? 
Feel free to order him around.

07:34.210 --> 07:35.850
Hey, where's the translation?

07:37.220 --> 07:40.720
Well, hang in there, little bro.

07:43.160 --> 07:44.580
See you, Yuki-chan.

07:44.980 --> 07:47.590
I'll make sure to brush up on my sign.

07:56.760 --> 08:00.380
<i>Oushi-kun, you're still studying sign?</i>

08:00.940 --> 08:02.210
Yeah.

08:02.890 --> 08:06.330
<i>I think I might want to be 
a sign language interpreter.</i>

08:07.150 --> 08:08.890
<i>Aren't I amazing?</i>

08:09.290 --> 08:11.130
<i>Yeah! That's awesome!</i>

08:11.450 --> 08:14.520
<i>It's usually women who take 
more of an interest in sign.</i>

08:16.860 --> 08:17.560
<i>Hmm?</i>

08:18.460 --> 08:19.310
<i>What?</i>

08:20.450 --> 08:24.020
Praise me more.

08:27.860 --> 08:30.380
<i>I'll be going, then.</i>

08:30.380 --> 08:32.430
<i>I'm glad I got to see Mio-san again.</i>

08:38.620 --> 08:41.250
<i>Have you met that dude lately?</i>

08:41.910 --> 08:43.540
<i>"That dude"?</i>

08:44.120 --> 08:45.620
<b>That dude</b>

08:44.230 --> 08:47.800
<i>Itsuomi-san? Are you two friends or something?</i>

08:47.800 --> 08:49.040
Hell no!

08:53.550 --> 08:57.010
His place...

08:58.100 --> 09:04.310
Have you been staying over there and stuff?

09:07.160 --> 09:11.750
<i>Oushi-kun, I don't know what expression 
you're asking me that with.</i>

09:16.550 --> 09:18.820
<i>Why did you sign looking down?</i>

09:19.870 --> 09:21.490
<i>So, what's the answer?</i>

09:22.540 --> 09:24.250
<i>I haven't stayed over.</i>

09:24.590 --> 09:25.320
Huh...

09:28.920 --> 09:30.250
<i>Don't overthink it.</i>

09:30.590 --> 09:36.810
<i>I just don't like the idea of some weirdo 
taking advantage of your disability.</i>

09:37.510 --> 09:39.620
<i>As your childhood friend.</i>

09:47.250 --> 09:50.740
<i>I wasn't overthinking it or anything.</i>

09:53.160 --> 09:56.830
<i>For Oushi-kun, it's not about me.</i>

09:56.830 --> 10:02.450
<i>He just really hates the idea of his sympathy 
for the deaf being misunderstood.</i>

10:03.410 --> 10:07.450
<i>He's been saying it for years, 
and he'll probably keep saying it.</i>

10:08.370 --> 10:11.900
<i>But, like, there's no need for him to.</i>

10:20.100 --> 10:23.680
What's wrong, Emma? 
Why are you sighing at your phone?

10:23.680 --> 10:26.600
Huh? No way, did I just sigh?

10:26.600 --> 10:28.560
Sure did. Boyfriend?

10:28.560 --> 10:30.940
N-N-No, no!

10:30.940 --> 10:37.190
I'll be home tonight.

10:30.940 --> 10:37.190
Today

10:30.940 --> 10:37.190
Been a while, Itsu-kun <3

10:30.940 --> 10:37.190
Let's go drinking sometime!

10:30.940 --> 10:37.190
Any places you want to check out?

10:31.400 --> 10:34.480
Wow, he hasn't replied for a week?

10:34.480 --> 10:37.190
He's probably traveling or something.

10:37.640 --> 10:39.970
This is nothing new for him.

10:39.970 --> 10:42.370
Then why let it bother you?

10:42.370 --> 10:44.880
He'll get back to you at some point.

10:44.880 --> 10:47.050
If he's into you, that is.

10:48.550 --> 10:51.410
C'mon, your customer will be here soon.

10:52.810 --> 10:53.850
Emma!

10:53.850 --> 10:55.960
Oh... Coming!

10:58.450 --> 11:00.310
<i>Message from Itsuomi-san!</i>

11:02.010 --> 11:04.850
Lake Tonlé Sap




There's shops and even
a school on the water.

11:07.010 --> 11:10.490
<i>He's surrounded by kids again.</i>

11:11.980 --> 11:14.480
Yuki, send me
a sign video.

11:17.230 --> 11:19.900
Yuki, send me
\ha sign video.

11:17.610 --> 11:23.740
Do you have time for it?

11:19.780 --> 11:23.740
Yeah.

11:21.780 --> 11:23.740
I'll make time.

11:24.060 --> 11:26.660
<i>I'll put on some makeup 
and take a video later.</i>

11:26.740 --> 11:31.250
So, hey

11:29.000 --> 11:31.250
It all happened so last minute...

11:31.250 --> 11:37.920
It all happened so last minute...

11:31.710 --> 11:37.920
But, uh... Here's to
\ha good relationship.

11:33.970 --> 11:37.810
<i>Last minute or not, I'm delighted 
to be going out with you.</i>

11:37.920 --> 11:40.630
Let me know if anything bothers you
\hor gives you trouble.

11:43.760 --> 11:48.770
<b>I was hoping to make
you laugh again</b>

11:45.430 --> 11:48.770
<i>S-Sorry! Please don't touch my tummy again!</i>

11:48.770 --> 11:51.390
Please don't touch
\hmy tummy again!

11:49.310 --> 11:53.020
Got it.

11:51.310 --> 11:53.020
But I can touch
you elsewhere?

11:56.060 --> 12:00.780
That's fine.

11:58.570 --> 12:00.780
I'll take good care of you.

12:03.220 --> 12:08.790
<i>The sky to the west is dyed orange 
in the corner of my eyes.</i>

12:09.430 --> 12:12.790
<i>I love these beautiful moments.</i>

12:12.910 --> 12:17.290
When I get back

12:14.790 --> 12:17.290
I'll make time for us.

12:17.540 --> 12:20.090
You can get clingy with me.

12:22.610 --> 12:26.590
<i>Why is the sky in my world so enormous?</i>

12:27.950 --> 12:32.750
<i>Will this twilight shining down on me 
soon shine down on you as well?</i>

12:36.050 --> 12:37.460
<i>Itsuomi-san...</i>

12:39.390 --> 12:42.110
<i>I miss you.</i>

12:45.130 --> 12:48.400
<i>It's been a month since 
Itsuomi-san left on his trip.</i>

12:48.400 --> 12:54.080
<i>At times, I wouldn't hear from him for days, 
but then he'd give me a full recap.</i>

12:55.750 --> 12:59.450
There was a festival in Thailand. 
Makha Bucha.

12:59.450 --> 13:01.680
It happens on a full moon day 
around this time of year.

13:02.850 --> 13:04.400
Made it to Myanmar.

13:04.400 --> 13:06.750
Here's me having a pint 
with a friend I made here.

13:08.050 --> 13:09.680
They were selling birds.

13:09.680 --> 13:11.850
You can buy them and set them free for karma.

13:12.690 --> 13:13.850
I did it.

13:14.650 --> 13:16.960
<i>And then, he went off the grid again.</i>

13:16.960 --> 13:18.860
<i>He was in India last.</i>

13:18.860 --> 13:23.860
Late at night on Indian trains,
tea vendors walk around
saying "Chai..." in a low voice.

13:19.430 --> 13:22.790
<i>I scroll down and see countries 
I know nothing about,</i>

13:22.790 --> 13:27.350
<i>all while my familiar hometown 
flows by outside the train window.</i>

13:27.350 --> 13:31.000
<i>It almost makes our relationship 
feel otherworldly.</i>

13:32.160 --> 13:32.870
<i>Hmm?</i>

13:32.870 --> 13:33.910
<b>Mailbox</b>

13:32.870 --> 13:33.910
<b>Inbox</b>

13:33.870 --> 13:35.750
<b>Inbox</b>

13:33.870 --> 13:35.830
<b>Mirror Inc. HR Kawai

Interview Result</b>

13:35.750 --> 13:39.130
<b>Sender: Mirror Inc. HR Kawai</b>

13:35.750 --> 13:39.130
<b>Recipient: Itose Yuki</b>

13:35.750 --> 13:39.130
<b>Interview Result</b>

13:35.750 --> 13:39.130
<b>Thank you for interviewing with us.
After careful consideration, we regret to inform
you that we will be going in another direction</b>

13:42.230 --> 13:47.520
<i>I wish Itsuomi-san would appear 
before me right now...</i>

13:51.890 --> 13:57.770
Good night

13:51.890 --> 13:57.810
Yeah, I'll text you

13:51.890 --> 13:57.810
Today

13:51.890 --> 13:57.810
Where are you?

13:52.190 --> 13:53.600
<i>Itsuomi-san?</i>

13:53.600 --> 13:55.400
<i>Huh? Now?</i>

13:55.060 --> 13:59.400
I'm back

13:57.690 --> 13:59.400
Wanna get lunch?

13:59.720 --> 14:01.390
<i>He's back?</i>

14:01.390 --> 14:03.400
<i>What? I can see him now?</i>

14:09.070 --> 14:10.990
I'm near college.

14:09.340 --> 14:12.580
<i>When did he get back?</i>

14:11.830 --> 14:13.740
Meet up at the station?

14:12.580 --> 14:15.620
<i>I figured it'd be soon...</i>

14:14.330 --> 14:16.250
I'll head out

14:15.620 --> 14:17.800
<i>But this is so out of the blue!</i>

14:17.080 --> 14:19.000
From home?
I'll meet you halfway!

14:19.940 --> 14:23.300
<i>I can finally see Itsuomi-san again!</i>

14:40.510 --> 14:41.920
<i>Itsuomi-san.</i>

14:58.410 --> 14:59.750
Yu

14:59.960 --> 15:01.290
ki

15:05.420 --> 15:08.010
I want to hug you.

15:06.070 --> 15:09.090
<i>"I want to hug you. Do you mind?"</i>

15:07.010 --> 15:09.090
Do you mind?

15:16.890 --> 15:19.060
Okay.

15:56.840 --> 15:57.520
<i>Huh?</i>

15:59.000 --> 15:59.890
<i>What?!</i>

16:04.150 --> 16:07.650
<b>KISS  KISS  KISS  KISS  KISS  KISS  KISS  KISS  KISS  KISS  KISS  KISS  KISS  KISS  KISS  KISS  KISS</b>

16:04.550 --> 16:07.650
<i>D-Did he just kiss me? Wha?</i>

16:08.190 --> 16:09.320
<i>Wait, what?</i>

16:09.570 --> 16:13.990
<i>Oh, was he not asking about a hug...</i>

16:13.150 --> 16:13.410
Okay.

16:14.360 --> 16:14.660
Do you mind?

16:14.530 --> 16:14.820
I want to hug you.

16:15.570 --> 16:22.660
I want to hug you.

16:17.120 --> 16:22.660
Do you mind?

16:18.870 --> 16:22.660
<b>X</b>

16:18.870 --> 16:22.660
(gyuu)

16:19.090 --> 16:20.440
<i>but a kiss?!</i>

16:19.160 --> 16:22.660
I want to kiss you.

16:19.160 --> 16:22.660
I want to kiss you.

16:19.160 --> 16:22.660
(chuu)

16:19.160 --> 16:22.660
(chuu)

16:20.440 --> 16:22.660
<i>I misread his lips because 
they share the same vowel!</i>

16:24.370 --> 16:28.600
<i>That was my first-ever kiss, 
and this is how it goes...</i>

16:28.600 --> 16:32.170
<i>You're looking at me like 
nothing even happened.</i>

16:32.890 --> 16:35.000
<i>What are you playing at?</i>

16:36.750 --> 16:40.600
Okay, let's go. 
I'm craving some Japanese food.

16:41.220 --> 16:45.800
<i>Why does he keep launching 
surprise bazookas at me?</i>

16:46.590 --> 16:49.250
<i>My heart feels like it's going to explode...</i>

16:50.800 --> 16:53.350
<i>His hair's a bit longer.</i>

16:54.460 --> 16:57.450
<i>And he's got a tan now.</i>

17:03.420 --> 17:06.000
<i>C-Calm down, me!</i>

17:06.820 --> 17:10.250
<i>It feels like he's grown 
a lot in our time apart.</i>

17:11.180 --> 17:12.760
<i>Itsuomi-san...</i>

17:21.350 --> 17:22.550
Yuki-san?

17:24.380 --> 17:28.020
And a silver-haired boy?

17:34.880 --> 17:36.730
Here's your order.

17:36.730 --> 17:39.030
Oh, thank you.

17:39.030 --> 17:41.530
<b>Soba Restaurant Kouan</b>

17:41.790 --> 17:46.000
<i>This is actually the first time 
we've gone anywhere to eat together.</i>

17:48.500 --> 17:53.170
I... re...com...mend... this.

17:52.000 --> 17:53.170
<b>Soba w/ Fried Tofu</b>

17:54.100 --> 17:55.790
<i>Fingerspelling!</i>

17:55.790 --> 17:58.430
<i>So he learned it during his trip.</i>

17:58.680 --> 18:02.060
We'll have a soba with fried tofu, 
and a cold soba.

18:02.060 --> 18:03.180
Sure.

18:07.270 --> 18:11.690
Fingerspelling makes it a lot 
easier to communicate.

18:12.340 --> 18:14.350
I gotta practice it more.

18:17.060 --> 18:26.470
We...l?...co...me... b...a...ck.

18:28.690 --> 18:32.350
<i>"Good to be home."</i>

18:38.550 --> 18:44.830
<i>The guy who was traveling the world 
yesterday is now eating before me.</i>

18:44.830 --> 18:47.100
Yeah, Japanese food hits the spot.

18:50.220 --> 18:54.000
<i>It's like I've got him all to myself here.</i>

18:57.500 --> 18:59.110
Don't worry. I got it.

18:59.110 --> 19:02.210
<i>Huh? He's paying for me, too?</i>

19:03.180 --> 19:04.370
It's fine.

19:05.150 --> 19:08.150
<i>I really need a job, and soon.</i>

19:13.040 --> 19:14.340
Come back!

19:25.390 --> 19:27.640
I've got something
important to talk about

19:29.020 --> 19:34.150
I want to introduce you
to this guy

19:31.270 --> 19:34.150
Shin.

19:34.400 --> 19:36.400
<i>Huh? Like the front of the leg?</i>

19:37.780 --> 19:40.150
The guy who came to the
bar drunk that one time

19:39.470 --> 19:43.010
<i>Oh, the guy who was with Emma-san back then.</i>

19:43.760 --> 19:44.990
<i>Right, Shin-san.</i>

19:46.280 --> 19:48.790
I want to introduce you to him
before anyone else

19:53.040 --> 19:59.050
Would you be okay
meeting him now?

19:55.040 --> 19:59.050
Or would you not?

19:57.370 --> 19:58.550
<i>Now...</i>

20:04.300 --> 20:07.560
I don't mind.

20:06.550 --> 20:07.560
But...

20:07.560 --> 20:10.270
I don't mind.

20:07.560 --> 20:10.270
But...

20:10.140 --> 20:11.810
It's a little scary.

20:14.470 --> 20:16.310
Is this about your hearing?

20:17.260 --> 20:19.500
<i>He's right, but I feel 
like I shouldn't admit it.</i>

20:20.290 --> 20:24.210
<i>He's offering to introduce me 
to a close friend.</i>

20:27.200 --> 20:28.990
Forget I said anything.

20:29.080 --> 20:32.080
Not that he's the judgy type...

20:35.080 --> 20:39.090
It's fine!!
Let's go see him!!

20:37.130 --> 20:39.090
Huh? You sure?

20:39.340 --> 20:43.840
Please introduce me
to Shin-san.

20:44.910 --> 20:47.100
Let's hold hands.

20:48.160 --> 20:51.350
Give me a squeeze if you want to leave.

20:57.220 --> 20:59.110
<i>It's begun.</i>

20:59.640 --> 21:02.880
<i>I want him to take me into his world.</i>

21:03.990 --> 21:06.650
<i>I want to learn more and have him learn more.</i>

21:07.710 --> 21:08.370
<i>But...</i>

21:09.220 --> 21:14.110
<i>I'd rather he not notice what a pain it'll be 
to hold my hand through it all just yet.</i>

21:26.840 --> 21:28.640
Yeet!

21:28.640 --> 21:30.650
Huh? This your girl?

21:30.650 --> 21:32.890
No way, for real?!

21:39.290 --> 21:40.750
Heya, Shin.

21:44.090 --> 21:46.400
You got here quick, Itsu-kun.

21:46.840 --> 21:47.920
<i>Huh?</i>

21:47.920 --> 21:51.500
<i>Oh, that was just how he is when drunk.</i>

21:54.820 --> 21:56.310
Who might this be?

21:56.310 --> 21:58.300
Let me introduce you...

22:02.050 --> 22:03.300
to my girlfriend.

22:07.000 --> 22:08.000
Girlfriend...?

23:15.080 --> 23:30.300
One Small Step
